§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDAnd they continued three years without war between Syria and Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd it came to pass in the third year, that Jehoshaphat the king of Judah came down to the king of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAnd the king of Israel said unto his servants, Know ye that Ramoth in Gilead is ours, and we be still, and take it not out of the hand of the king of Syria?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾And he said unto Jehoshaphat, Wilt thou go with me to battle to Ramoth-gilead? And Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, I am as thou art, my people as thy people, my horses as thy horses.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcAnd Jehoshaphat said unto the king of Israel, Enquire, I pray thee, at the word of the LORD to day.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book
§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙòThen the king of Israel gathered the prophets together, about four hundred men, and said unto them, Shall I go against Ramoth-gilead to battle, or shall I forbear? And they said, Go up; for the Lord shall deliver it into the hand of the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdAnd Jehoshaphat said, Is there not here a prophet of the LORD besides, that we might enquire of him?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ÷And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, There is yet one man, Micaiah the son of Imlah, by whom we may enquire of the LORD: but I hate him; for he doth not prophesy good concerning me, but evil. And Jehoshaphat said, Let not the king say so.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\Then the king of Israel called an officer, and said, Hasten hither Micaiah the son of Imlah.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
